{
 "reference": "Two real PMS 1.43.4.10903, both online, each with the harness clips (harness/scripts/make-media.sh) in a Movies library: `unclaimed` is plexlab on kids (claimed=\"0\" since 2026-10-22), `claimed` a throwaway pms-docker container on kids claimed to a test account without Plex Pass for this recording, then signed out and its plex.tv device deleted. Each was sent python-plexapi's request shapes below with curl from inside its container (the owner's token on the claimed one), collection made by plexapi's createCollection request; bodies are the JSON answers, Metadata of the film's own agent candidates dropped.",
 "date": "2026-11-04",
 "client": "python-plexapi 4.18.2 (Kometa calls 4.18.3; these methods are unchanged), recorded through a requests response hook on PlexServer._session while it ran createCollection, logos, uploadLogo(filepath=, url=), setLogo, uploadTheme(filepath=), themes, sortUpdate('alpha'/'custom'), reload and a film's uploadLogo(url=) against rex (9f7d8bdc refused the uploads, so setLogo and sortUpdate('custom')'s PUT were recorded against the fix; the shapes are plexapi's whatever the answer); the filepath uploads are a 1x1 PNG the recorder made; `plexapi` keeps each call's method, path and body length. Kometa (modules/plex.py, builder.py) reaches these through upload_logo and collection_order_query (rex#15).",
 "findings": [
  "collectionSort's enumValues is '0:Release date|1:Alphabetical|2:Custom' on the claimed server and '0:Release date|1:Alphabetical' on the unclaimed one; both store and read back 2.",
  "POST .../clearLogos?url= and .../themes?url= on a collection: empty 200, upload://{clearLogos,themes}/<sha1 of the fetched bytes>, listed newest first and selected; the row gains Image type clearLogo /library/metadata/{id}/clearLogo/{v}, a theme attribute, and locked clearLogo/theme Fields.",
  "Any bytes the url answers are kept (a GitHub README, its own /identity); a url it cannot fetch is 406 (a poster's is 502); no url and no body 406.",
  "PUT .../clearLogos?url= and .../themes?url= are 404 on a collection and a film alike; python-plexapi's setLogo sends PUT .../clearLogo?url=<ratingKey>, 200 with the new path as its body; without url 400.",
  "A film's POST /library/metadata/1/clearLogos?url= is 200."
 ],
